{
  "id": "26854_bakageru",
  "headword": "{馬鹿|ばか}げる",
  "reading": "ばかげる",
  "romaji": "bakageru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to be ridiculous; to be absurd; to be foolish",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be ridiculous; to be absurd; to be foolish",
      "explanation": "To be so silly, illogical, or unreasonable as to not deserve serious consideration. Almost always used in the past participle form ばかげた (ridiculous, absurd) as a modifier."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "26854_bakageru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{馬鹿|ばか}げた{話|はなし}だ。",
      "english": "That's a ridiculous story.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26854_bakageru_ex2",
      "japanese": "そんな{馬鹿|ばか}げたことはやめなさい。",
      "english": "Stop doing such ridiculous things.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26854_bakageru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{馬鹿|ばか}げた{値段|ねだん}で{売|う}られている。",
      "english": "It's being sold at an absurd price.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26854_bakageru_ex4",
      "japanese": "こんな{馬鹿|ばか}げた{規則|きそく}に{従|したが}う{必要|ひつよう}はないと{思|おも}う。",
      "english": "I don't think we need to follow such a ridiculous rule.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Almost exclusively used in the form {馬鹿|ばか}げた + noun (as an adjectival modifier) or {馬鹿|ばか}げている (to be ridiculous). The bare dictionary form {馬鹿|ばか}げる rarely appears on its own. Expresses dismissive contempt for something considered beneath serious consideration.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {馬鹿|ばか}げた{話|はなし}: ridiculous story\n- {馬鹿|ばか}げた{考|かんが}え: absurd idea\n- {馬鹿|ばか}げた{行為|こうい}: foolish act\n- {馬鹿|ばか}げた{質問|しつもん}: ridiculous question\n- {馬鹿|ばか}げている: to be ridiculous\n\nUSAGE:\nThe ta-form ({馬鹿|ばか}げた) functions as an adjective modifying nouns. This pattern is common for certain verbs whose participle has become more frequent than the base form.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- くだらない: worthless, stupid — emphasizes something being not worth one's time\n- ばからしい: foolish, absurd — similar meaning, less formal\n- {呆|あき}れる: to be astonished — reaction of disbelief at someone's foolishness",
